" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/assets/333a99cd7b1f4aa0c3017c2b5aa42cb04acad842b19345a1176d57a71c5fd120.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=-{sec}^{2}⁡x$, the $x$-axis and the lines $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$, as shown above. Find the area of the region." :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}(-{sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x{|}_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{4})) \\\\  & =-(1-(-1)) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-73324/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ad216da-1bcf-5b87-9436-918ef1e5015a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73324"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-345343/field-1/9ab64b945e95c1c3798cea70f4ae7ad55133b01b9b894848e70b56c91ffbae97" :answer/id #uuid "25f991f6-3353-56a2-83b3-1b27ebe7a8a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186287007 :answer-field/choices ["q-345343/field-1/9ab64b945e95c1c3798cea70f4ae7ad55133b01b9b894848e70b56c91ffbae97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-345343"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/assets/34eb73b6bd93f9a45b666ed0599719a09b54948d1d81b14ceea9b46f99b75054.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y=-{x}^{2}-1$, the $x$-axis, and the line $x=-1$ and $x=1$ (shown above). Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-54471/selection/29e18d29d5a8d00489a807deb821c9d8fb2c816d74392c4ec1d541f26b369225" :answer/id #uuid "e201c8fd-1869-5ede-b6ad-0aed0618b063" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{16}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-54471/selection/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8" :answer/id #uuid "69c92cc3-1574-57cc-8792-762701e9886e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-54471/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer/id #uuid "2e68784f-1248-5cb6-84f2-9859e21acd00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-54471/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "24eb3c35-0b2a-59b8-93bf-0aa48f818997" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-54471/selection/5c0598f19f8324c341654ad8fd4df667dbb52f406431a30b6711906dc66d3ee4" :answer/id #uuid "c20809de-5f82-506a-904c-5a4896f05924" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-54471/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1c2c475a-8897-55ec-8804-225f2b7be9a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-54471/selection/5c0598f19f8324c341654ad8fd4df667dbb52f406431a30b6711906dc66d3ee4" :answer-field/choices ["q-54471/selection/29e18d29d5a8d00489a807deb821c9d8fb2c816d74392c4ec1d541f26b369225" "q-54471/selection/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8" "q-54471/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" "q-54471/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-54471/selection/5c0598f19f8324c341654ad8fd4df667dbb52f406431a30b6711906dc66d3ee4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-54471" :question/id #uuid "882a6182-51b5-5a78-824c-d594efd5fdfc" :question/math-academy-id "q-54471" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/assets/d07ef9eb8b578cd9f5f0c2c57caa44760b0a5e21d95bb0961fcff722276a7b4e.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y={x}^{2}-4$, the $x$-axis and the line $x=-2$ and $x=2$, shown above." :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}({x}^{2}-4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-4{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{-2}^{2}-4x{|}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{2}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{(-2)^{3}}{3})-4(2+2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{32}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $\\frac{32}{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-54471/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ad216da-1bcf-5b87-9436-918ef1e5015a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-54471"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-406820/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "797e665b-c83f-5bae-bfb9-18eaa7f1cfea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-406820/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "4cc25586-ebac-5b08-92c1-0da3e689842a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-406820/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "96ab2319-8b24-5616-a0b6-4e7b27e531ba" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-406820/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-406820/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-406820/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-406820" :question/id #uuid "1ce635ef-dd49-5b27-ab90-ab2605396353" :question/math-academy-id "q-406820" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/assets/31db08aa86f46d6601820b34dd938bc4b3738cba90f2fdd2721b4eb2069fa40b.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$, the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$, as shown above. Find the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}(-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡x{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =1-2 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is \n\n$$\nA=-{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-406820/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ad216da-1bcf-5b87-9436-918ef1e5015a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-406820"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-103824"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/assets/97cf633bce7a8eeef443757e62d52f356c911b6aee3d8019d434d514416b0049.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and the $x$-axis between $x=-\\pi $ and $x=0$, as shown above. What is the area of the region?" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-781"] :question/problem "Find the area between the curve $y=x^2-2x+2,$ the $x$-axis, and the lines $x=0$ and $x=2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/assets/6b85f10cde49017eac1c56ad1b8abbcdf3033a367d5e1eb162dd89fbb6141461.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-782"] :question/worked-solution "First, we find the intersections of the curve with the $x$-axis:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-1 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1 \\\\ x & =\\pm 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe draw a sketch of the region, as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/assets/9b78aad41f84f6a6997914bd8d4243f30cb0ebea4edb5305962dc11c7a46a807.png)\n\nWe want the area between the curve $y=x^2-1$ and the $x$-axis, from $x=-1$ to $x=1.$ To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}({x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{-1}^{1}-x{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{3}-(-\\frac{1}{3}))-(1-(-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}-2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $\\dfrac{4}{3}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
